# She'll be comin' 'round the mountain - Amerikaans volkslied
# Traditioneel; afgeleid van de spiritual "When the Chariot Comes" (gedrukt 1899) en
# door spoorwegarbeiders in de jaren 1890 aangepast (Wikipedia (en), "She'll Be Coming
# 'Round the Mountain"). Publiek domein. De inleidende strofe over Billy Hill staat in de
# bladmuziek "She'll be comin' round the mountain when she comes" (Robbins Music Corp., New
# York, 1932), met als componist Hugo Frey (1873-1952); een tekstdichter wordt daar niet
# genoemd (UW-Madison, Popular Sheet Music Collection, record pop001956). Meld het als u de
# tekstdichter van die strofe kent.
# Overgenomen uit SHELLBEC.OMI (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991). De bron noemt als melodie "Tante uit
# Marokko"; dat Nederlandse lied (ik-heb-een-tante-in-marokko) gaat op deze wijs.
{title: She'll be comin' 'round the mountain}
{meta: id she-ll-be-comin-round-the-mountain}
{meta: language en}
{lyricist: traditioneel}
{composer: traditioneel}
{copyright: Public domain}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: source Overgenomen uit SHELLBEC.OMI (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991); herkomst via Wikipedia (en), She'll Be Coming 'Round the Mountain; inleidende strofe via UW-Madison Popular Sheet Music Collection, pop001956}
{meta: tag kampvuur}
{meta: tag volkslied}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: Inleiding}
[F]Billy Hill, a hillybill, an old [C7]rail road man
When he'd hear a whistle or a bell
[D7]He'd start in to roar
sounds [Gm]like engine fortyfour
[G7]Then the neighbours all would hear him [C7]yell
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
She'll be comin' [F]'round the mountain, when she comes
She'll be comin' [F]'round the mountain, when she comes
I can hear [F]that engine pan[F7]tin'
And the passen[Bb]gers a chan[G7]tin'
[C7]She'll be comin' 'round the [F]mountain, when she comes
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
She'll be drivin' six white horses, when she comes
She'll be drivin' six white horses, when she comes
When you hear that whistle tootin'
You can gamble sure as shootin'
She'll be drivin' six white horses, when she comes
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
She'll be comin' 'round the mountain, when she comes
She'll be comin' 'round the mountain, when she comes
If she hits a cow on Sunday
Then we'll all have beef steak Monday
She'll be comin' 'round the mountain, when she comes
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
She'll be comin' 'round the mountain, when she comes
She'll be comin' 'round the mountain, when she comes
We will kill the old red rooster
And we'll all have chicken and dumplin'
O we'll all go to meet her, when she comes
{end_of_verse}
